.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# The icon source drop. 80 stock packs, 124 MB, and only about 11 MB of it is
# servable: each pack ships an Illustrator source and an EPS alongside the svg/
# and png/ folders, and nobody downloading an icon from a web page opens a .ai.
#
# tools/icons-sync.py copies the svg/ and png/ files out of here into
# assets/icons/, which IS committed. So this folder is a working input, not the
# asset store — you need it to add or re-sync packs, and not to build or serve
# the site. Keep the original download somewhere backed up: it is the only copy
# of the vector sources, and it is not in this repository.
/icons/

# The photography drop. Fifty Adobe Stock comps still under their download names
# (1000_F_<id>_<hash>.webp). They are copied into assets/images/shortlist/ as
# <adobe-id>.webp, which IS committed, because that is the name the cards look for.
# Keeping both would commit the same 3.5 MB twice under two naming schemes and
# leave no way to tell which one the site actually reads. Same arrangement as
# /icons/ above: a working input, not the asset store.
/photography/

# Adobe Stock API key. A credential — never commit it.
/.adobe-stock-key
